{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D141-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ce391eb57d66838d0793dc16a34b3b909f60cf4143a3767f5c350c441ba5a67d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 offers no meeting facts, so A5's 'Lovely people' does not clearly reveal less.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 evades B2's question; B4 changes the question but barely changes A5's tea tactic.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek information, but neither establishes why this meeting matters to B.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats A1's tea offer without a clear further contraction of disclosure.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a meeting and tea, but no particular relationship or consequence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's reassurance and A5's tea are concise but familiar evasions.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 57\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your school meeting went fine, love. The headteacher and I discussed your suspension. Have some tea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How long am I suspended?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A little while. I'll be home with you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Will I miss the school play?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Oh, sweetheart. Come sit beside me. You don't have to face this alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A meets successive questions with progressively less information while maintaining affectionate availability and reassurance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic evasion can avoid questions without progressively reducing disclosure or sustaining care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"The revision moves from A1's named suspension to A3's vague duration to A5's information-free comfort.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses parental protection and a child's concrete loss; alternative b uses a service worker's accommodating reassurance.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the unspecified meeting with a school suspension. B4's feared loss prompts greater comfort and zero factual disclosure. Separate internal reread scores, in rubric order: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The parent's withholding can read as patronizing; A5 needs sincere concern rather than a smug refusal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D141-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bbc36e3cf6d83c75989adf610d4e82e49a4947d5695bb03dff547f3d68109683\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Somewhere being handled' contracts to A5's 'Someone,' with continued hospitality.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's 'By whom?' directly follows A3's 'being handled' and receives a narrower answer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the parcel located, but B4 supplies no practical pressure or personal stake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 reduces disclosure, though 'Someone' is only slightly emptier than A3.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a missing parcel but leaves A's role and ability to help unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's biscuit offer economically replaces the requested handler's identity.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your wedding dress reached our depot this morning. Please sit; I'll look after you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Which depot? I'll collect it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"One of ours. Let me save you a wasted journey.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can you at least give me their number?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You have me, and I'm staying right here with you.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A substitutes increasingly complete personal reassurance for increasingly unavailable factual answers.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Customer-service obstruction alone need not preserve warmth or reveal progressively less.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 gives a location category and arrival time, A3 only an affiliation, and A5 only companionship.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike alternative a's parental comfort, this worker accommodates the customer emotionally while closing practical routes to collection.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a delivery-service encounter with a wedding dress. B4 requests a smaller actionable detail, causing A5 to offer only personal presence. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 may sound institutionally sinister if played mechanically; its caring promise must remain sincere.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D142-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"95839eb199eed8d3e4babdef300d07f65d3d168626d5bb2b42d70e9f3d2260b7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices a name against a truth, but A5 reduces the purchased name to a surname without explaining equality.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's claim of knowledge as proof of stock; A5 prices B4's offered caller identity.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 bargains, but B2 never clarifies what B needs the name for.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 subdivides the product but does not establish why the offer merits only a surname.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'useful name' and B4's 'who called' lack a playable shared situation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'product exists' makes the information market clear in a short reply.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll name the coworker who reported your lateness if you name whoever reported mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I only know which department.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll trade departments. Names cost names.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Payroll. But I can introduce you to my source.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Marketing. And I'll arrange coffee with mine. Same access, same price.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assigns information and access explicit exchange values and matches each offered item with an equivalent.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary bargaining can seek advantage without requiring equal value for each fact or introduction.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 matches departments to departments; A5 separately reciprocates B4's fact and offered introduction.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a is a cooperative exchange between coworkers; alternative b values confessions according to consequences within a family.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced reciprocal workplace reporting. B4 upgrades the offer to access, so A5 supplies both a matching fact and introduction. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The explicit pricing language is slightly demonstrative, although the coworkers have a credible reason to use it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D142-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5cb4160a8c364faab5f99d34de31fe49c03eb8296fd6f3495799b8c8db039238\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands a secret, but A3 gives a complimentary confession and A5 never identifies equal value.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's pricing objection; A5 answers B4's request for the rest with subscription terms.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 objects morally, but B4 abandons that concern without adding concrete leverage.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 enlarges the sales metaphor without developing an actual exchange of secrets.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a stolen key but no owner, purpose, or consequence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's subscription line is compact but could end many unrelated transactional scenes.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll tell you why I took Mum's spare key if you admit something that could get you grounded too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I broke her mug.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's a weekend. This key is a month. Have you got anything bigger?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I lent her car to Jamie.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A month each, then. I used the key to let Jamie move into her flat.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats confession as an asset whose price must be met by an equally consequential confession.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Mutual blackmail uses secrets as threats; this exchange instead negotiates equivalent disclosure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 rejects the mug confession as insufficient payment, and A5 releases the secret after B4 raises the stakes.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b bargains over family punishment and shared exposure; alternative a exchanges workplace information and introductions.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced siblings and their mother's spare key. B4 supplies the larger confession A3 requested, earning A5's reciprocal disclosure. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The month-for-month valuation is A's sincere estimate; the scene should not imply that the mother has fixed sentencing rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D143-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6405e34f46828d2c41e6dd4457ba9b5c27cf6b3ba118e8f57f8d5d1bbeecbfe0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 narrows the disclosure obligation, but A3 stalls and A5 answers without narrowing it again.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 acknowledges B2's new question, and A5 finally answers after B4 insists.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 applies pressure with 'Answer it,' but B's connection to the box remains absent.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 ends the delay with 'Yes' and a maxim rather than a tighter honesty boundary.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 implies an inquiry and B2 supplies a box, but its significance is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains the precision joke instead of embodying a fresh restriction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 61\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll be honest about your missing donation box. You asked where I went; I said the bank.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Did you take the box there?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. You didn't ask what was inside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Was the money still in it when you arrived?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"At the car park, yes. If you mean the counter, that's a different arrival.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts honesty while repeatedly shrinking the scope and definitions of the answers owed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple withholding omits information; this card justifies omission by redefining what counts as an honest answer.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 excludes contents from the transport question, and A5 divides B4's 'arrived' into separate locations.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a exploits precise wording during an investigation; alternative b exploits who and what belong in a promised account.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified B's missing donation box and a bank visit. B4 closes the contents loophole, causing A5 to narrow the meaning of arrival. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The scene implies possible misconduct without resolving it; A should defend the answer's adequacy rather than advertise guilt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D143-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b2d787563e8c4f344c82fef20bb1382944368a95941af423a7acd936a2333b0c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 limits honesty to answers and A5 subdivides the requested company into arrival and departure lists.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's accusation by shifting responsibility; A5 uses B4's question about companions.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 objects to being misled, but B4 leaves the relationship and reason for asking unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 introduces a useful distinction but merely offers two lists rather than committing to a narrower account.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1's promise and B4's 'with you' provide no concrete event or setting.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Only if you stop asking' efficiently transfers the burden to B.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll be honest about my birthday. When you rang, I was eating dinner alone.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Your brother posted a photo from our kitchen.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"He came for dessert. By dinner, I mean the main course.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He's beside you while you're carving the chicken.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Carving isn't eating. I meant the moments when food was actually in my mouth.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts honesty while repeatedly shrinking the definitions and moments covered by the account.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A simple denial disputes the evidence; this behavior accepts the evidence while excluding it from what the honest statement covers.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 excludes dessert from dinner; after B4 supplies chicken carving, A5 excludes preparation from eating and counts only mouthfuls.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a narrows destinations and contents during an investigation; this alternative narrows a domestic account of shared company to individual eating moments.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the birthday and shared kitchen, replacing the cake-authorship dodge with a progressively narrower account. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 redefine dinner and eating; logic 5, B2's photo causes the dessert boundary and B4's chicken closes it; relationship 4, B2 and B4 challenge the account with household evidence; heightening 4, A5 reduces the account to mouthfuls; specificity 4, A1's birthday call and B4's carving establish the occasion; brevity/wit 4, A5's eating distinction embodies the evasion. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns; the exchange remains open.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 implies the brother was absent during actual mouthfuls without establishing that fact. A's sincere defense of this narrow claim must carry the loophole; B can still challenge it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D144-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d71a3f260cc9b6ddbefc3082d9902a3bd57595ab50e96866cc995e6d93959655\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 and A5 convert explanations into suspicion, but add neither identifiable people nor higher stakes.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 recasts B2's accidental loss as disappearance; A5 recasts B4's denial as coordination.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers an explanation and B4 resists, but neither establishes what B is trying to accomplish.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's coordinated refusal repeats A1's unnamed accomplice without enlarging the threat.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's missing receipt is playable, but the purchase and consequence remain undefined.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'They're improving' is an economical reversal of B2's mundane explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 63\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our toaster receipt is gone. The shop must have someone inside this house.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I probably recycled it. We can get a copy.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"So the recycling crew removes originals while the shop prints replacements.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Every shop prints replacement receipts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Every shop? Then it's the whole high street. We can't trust a single warranty.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns innocent explanations into evidence for an expanding network and a growing practical threat.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Persistent suspicion alone can keep accusing the same person without enlarging participation or stakes.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 recruits recycling workers; A5 uses B4's 'Every shop' to implicate the high street and all warranties.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a grows through a housemate's helpful repair suggestions; alternative b grows through a clerk's institutional explanations.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified a toaster return and shared household. B4 generalizes the harmless service, which A5 converts into a larger conspiracy and wider loss of protection. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The warranty stakes stay deliberately small; increasing earnest alarm should carry the expansion without requiring grandiose threats.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D144-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7127420dcbc17a034ff1e3edac8be40301e3596a62a9d67960be5792014847ec\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 says the story reached management although A1 already included the manager; A5 adds only a protocol.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 reinterprets B2's truth claim, and A5 treats B4's denial as organized procedure.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 defend an answer, but the answer's subject and B's practical interest are missing.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'denial protocol' increases rhetoric without adding people or consequences.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a manager but never identifies the disputed service or decision.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's protocol phrase neatly absorbs B4's denial into A's theory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 61\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You and your manager both say my train was cancelled. Who told you to match stories?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The signal failed. It's on the public departure board.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"They've recruited the board operators to stop me reaching the interview.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The same fault is delaying three counties.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Three counties to keep me unemployed. My replacement must already have government backing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats corroborating explanations as proof of additional conspirators pursuing an increasingly consequential scheme.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A persecution claim can remain static; this card requires each explanation to enlarge the network and stakes.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 adds board operators and interview sabotage; A5 converts B4's geographic scale into government-backed replacement.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b pits a traveller's personal theory against a clerk's wider service facts; alternative a builds from cooperative domestic troubleshooting.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a cancelled train and threatened interview. B4's three-county disruption causes A5's jump to national influence and permanent employment loss. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The government inference is a substantial leap; A must treat B4's scale as its evidentiary basis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D145-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0d84f29881d8398fe43c34045a5fe34099c70d443bc2f7873de8c9c6ba64d5f2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits B into dinner hospitality for a cupboard, and A3 adapts ordinary manners to its handle.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 solves B2's missing-lap problem; A5 affirms B4's soup offer but adds no practical next step.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 raises a hosting difficulty and B4 voluntarily proposes another hospitable act.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on normality rather than extending B4's proposed soup service.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's dinner, napkin and talking cupboard immediately establish playable domestic business.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'ordinary hospitality' explains the achieved effect instead of earning a further turn.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 83\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Pass the talking cupboard a napkin. Let's make dinner normal.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It doesn't have a lap.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then put it beside the handle, like a considerate host.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Should I offer it soup?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please. Ask which shelf it eats from. We can't keep making our guest explain everything.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits B into repeated practical hospitality toward something strange until participation becomes ordinary etiquette.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply accepting a talking cupboard does not require another person to help enact its normal treatment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks B to serve it, A3 solves B2's service problem, and revised A5 turns B4's soup offer into expected manners.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now makes B a considerate cohost; alternative b helps B move beyond a mistaken greeting to conversational inclusion.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the dinner setting and changed the explanatory ending. B4's soup offer now causes a specific serving question and greater commitment to hosting. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The shelf question assumes the cupboard can eat; the shared strange premise supports that assumption without establishing a new rule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D145-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"87718dde591c15df655eb33df3eb58166f584f553a1c915440aa7901072a0d99\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 recruits a greeting to an invisible guest; A5 extends B's participation into ordinary concern about comfort.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's eyeline problem with the chair; A5 develops B4's literal chair greeting into a guest-directed question.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 admits difficulty and B4 tries the solution, giving A a credible novice participant to help.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 advances from acknowledging presence to accommodating the guest's environmental preference.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes an invisible guest and A3 locates the guest in a chair, though the occasion is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's 'Hello, chair' earns A5's patient 'Good start' without an unrelated punchline.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our invisible dinner guest is here. Will you introduce Mum while I finish the gravy?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can't see where to look.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The chair beside you. Just introduce them as you normally would.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Hello, chair, this is Mum. She needs your seat.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Introduce her to the guest, love. Then fetch another chair; we can't ask someone to stand just because Mum can't see them.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits B into ordinary hosting duties toward an invisible guest and develops participation into practical accommodation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Teaching someone where to look can remain a demonstration; A instead needs B's help conducting a dinner with competing seating needs.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 delegates an introduction while cooking, A3 solves B2's visibility problem, and A5 converts B4's seat request into fetching additional seating.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The cupboard alternative develops voluntary soup service; this alternative turns a mistaken introduction and Mum's competing need into an ordinary obligation to seat everyone.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified a family dinner and A's cooking duty. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1 and A5 enlist introductions and seating; logic 5, B2 causes A3's eyeline and B4 causes A5's correction and extra chair; relationship 4, B4 advocates for Mum while A1 needs help; heightening 4, A5 makes the invisible guest's occupancy materially count; specificity 4, A1's gravy and B4's seat establish hosting business; brevity/wit 4, A5 applies ordinary seating fairness to invisibility. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns; no predetermined resolution.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 retains some instructional phrasing, but the gravy and seating problem give it an immediate domestic purpose. The invisible guest remains an asserted premise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D146-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b48fcd5fbc40a933c154a6c13dde4de406a6bcfec5c83f64f1396248ccdaa5c4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 keeps B present, but a visitor before sunset is not an impossible prediction, and A3 evades disproof.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's sunset with time zones; A5 responds to B4's 'Nobody' by broadening visitor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 offer reasons to leave, forcing A to find successive grounds for staying.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a definition dispute but gives no responsible method for resolving the prophecy.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies sunset and a visitor but leaves the impossible event and shared occasion unclear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's clipped 'Here' makes the time-zone loophole playable and economical.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay until sunset. Gran predicted this stone would hatch, and I promised we'd witness the result.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The sun's down. It's still a stone.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then help me record that it didn't hatch. We can put the prophecy to rest.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll sign, but Gran never said which day.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then stay while we ring her and agree a deadline. I can't witness every sunset alone.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A keeps B present by making departure depend on jointly resolving an impossible prediction.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Moving the goalposts indefinitely protects belief; this card also permits witnessed disproof or a responsible revision.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 accepts failure, while B4's genuine ambiguity causes A5 to seek an agreed deadline with Gran.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses a family promise and negotiated revision; alternative b uses practical documentation to establish disproof.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a hatching stone and family witness obligation. B4 exposes an unspecified date, causing A5 to retain B for a concrete revision process. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Calling Gran offers a route toward resolution; it should remain an immediate proposal, not a prescribed ending.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D146-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"38797f4f0e45f8a4ba595dfebafaaa00727047bb3d137ee5c5287883a900a817\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 delays departure and A3 pursues documented disproof after B2 establishes that no bell exists.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's absent bell, but A5's departure becoming prophecy does not follow clearly from B4's offer to write.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers to produce the requested evidence, materially enabling resolution.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 invokes an unexplained prophetic consequence instead of developing the offered documentation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a coat and bell, but the actual prediction and its timing remain vague.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's documented absence is concrete; A5's abstract departure clause obscures the final turn.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 66\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep your coat off. The prophecy says this bell-less tower will ring at noon; I need a witness.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's twelve-oh-one. We heard nothing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then sign that before you go. We can officially stop waiting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"My watch is five minutes fast.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then give me four more minutes. I'll fill in our names so only the silence needs witnessing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes B's continued presence necessary to establish whether an impossible prediction has failed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Arbitrary obstruction keeps someone waiting without a relevant condition; A ties waiting to the prediction's actual deadline.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised B4 corrects the clock, and A5 requests exactly the remaining four minutes while preparing the disproof record.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b accepts a finite evidentiary delay; alternative a discovers an open deadline and seeks a family-negotiated revision.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified an impossible tower bell and noon deadline. B4 invalidates premature disproof, causing A5's limited extension and practical preparation. Internal reread: 5,5,4,4,5,4 = 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The official document is A's personal demand; the dialogue does not establish any real authority behind it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D147-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7d7206b12378f7fabb3f589e0c6b01a9108f87489218a9ef47a68e2831bda11f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands an apology for sitting without the chair's agreement, an explicitly impossible expectation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 turns B2's objection into a reason for easy compliance; A5 challenges B4's unspecific apology.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 resists and B4 complies minimally, changing A's task from obtaining an apology to improving it.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 requires acknowledgment of the particular offense after B4 offers only 'Sorry, chair.'\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 immediately establishes someone sitting and the disputed lack of permission, though the location is open.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'For what?' precisely catches B4's perfunctory compliance before the furniture rationale.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before your caretaker interview, apologise to that chair. You sat without its consent.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It can't say yes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then tell it you're sorry for taking silence as permission.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sorry, chair. I'll stand for the interview.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then apologise for making it redundant. You're applying to care for furniture, and your first solution is to leave it without a job.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes B apologize for violating furniture's impossible consent requirement and expands the apology when B offers restitution.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A generic test of politeness could demand manners without an impossible injured party; A requires an apology to a chair that must consent to use yet retain its purpose.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 requires the chair's consent, A3 treats its silence as grounds for apology, and A5 converts B4's offer to stand into depriving the chair of work.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Both alternatives turn attempted repair into a further apology. This caretaker interview makes B's solution evidence of professional unfitness through the chair's lost purpose; the inn alternative treats advance telephone notice as a breach of the doorway's social priority.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the caretaker interview and replaced only the rejected candidate's final turn. B4's standing remedy now causes a specific additional grievance: leaving the chair without work. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5, A1 and A3 require apology for impossible consent and A5 renews apology to the same object; logic 5, B2's inability to consent causes A3's silence distinction and B4's standing causes A5's redundancy claim; relationship 4, A1's applicant wants to proceed and B4 offers accommodation that A5 judges against the job; heightening 4, A5 makes avoiding unauthorized use another injury with employment implications; specificity 4, A1 establishes the interview and chair, though A's exact hiring authority remains implicit; brevity/wit 4, A5's 'redundant' connects the proposed standing to the employment setting. Total = 30 + 20 + 12 + 12 + 8 + 8 = 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, 62 words; acceptance and the interview outcome remain open. This is an internal model reread, not human approval or live testing.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 interprets one unused seat as redundancy, an intentionally disproportionate account of the chair's purpose. The final employment criticism could overshadow the apology unless A's concern remains sincerely directed toward the chair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D147-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"760dec77d81dde4de158ff01d9f1081c86f61828311e7fef5f681adcdbc03421\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands an apology to a doorway, but B4's slamming is ordinary mistreatment rather than a clearly impossible expectation.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's lack of grudges as reassurance; A5 treats B4's apology as progress toward permission.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 objects but B4 cooperates, allowing A to advance the reconciliation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 moves to asking about visitors, partly leaving the apology objective behind.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's handle establishes an immediate access problem and B4 supplies the prior slamming.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'This should clear up quickly' efficiently turns B2's objection into encouragement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Welcome to our inn. Please apologise to the doorway for knocking after you arrived.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I had to get here to knock.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It expected advance notice from your knuckles. Explain that you're sorry.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sorry, doorway. I did phone ahead.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then apologise for telling the telephone first. It had to hear about its own visitor secondhand.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A seeks an apology for an object's impossible advance-notice expectation and treats B's attempted repair as another violation requiring apology.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Appeasing a personified door need not involve impossible expectations; this doorway expects a visitor's knuckles to announce arrival before reaching it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 requires a pre-arrival knock, A3 preserves that requirement despite B2's physical objection, and A5 turns B4's phone call into an additional precedence offense.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The chair alternative ties fuller apology to professional trust; this innkeeper treats a guest's helpful advance call as a further injury to the doorway's social priority.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced an inn arrival and replaced the unstable carrying-and-waiting ritual. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1 and A3 require apology for impossible advance knocking; logic 5, B2's travel objection prompts A3's knuckle requirement and B4's phone call causes A5's telephone offense; relationship 4, A1 hosts an arriving guest who attempts repair in B4; heightening 4, A5 converts that repair into a more specific apology; specificity 4, A1 supplies the inn threshold and arrival; brevity/wit 4, A5's secondhand notice follows exactly from B4. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, with admission and reconciliation unresolved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The doorway's reception of secondhand news is A's anthropomorphic interpretation. No actual telephone-to-door communication needs to be established or performed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D148-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d295f169874df987afecafbb58eb75bf4e5e23926db9f17fa05b961ec5e7310e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks approval for storing future rain, and A5 escalates temporal borrowing while requesting a signature.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 makes B2's unarrived Tuesday a storage advantage; A5 solves B4's overflow with Wednesday's saucer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 shifts from rejecting the premise to evaluating containment, giving A a practical approval obstacle.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends storing future weather into borrowing equipment from a later day.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies rain, Tuesday and a cup; the approving institution is left implicit.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'why we have room' turns the exact objection into a compact project advantage.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"As venue manager, will you approve storing Tuesday's rain in this cup? The wedding needs a dry lawn.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Tuesday hasn't happened.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. We'll catch the rain before it learns how to fall.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I have another wedding Wednesday. What if it leaks overnight?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll seal it with Thursday's drought. Sign for two dry weddings; I'll invoice the drought after it happens.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A pursues formal approval by answering practical objections with successively stranger explanations of weather and time.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Surreal invention alone can accumulate odd images; A uses each invention to address the approving manager's specific operational concerns.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 makes B2's future date permit catching untrained rain; A5 answers B4's overnight risk with a future drought seal and a renewed signature request.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative bargains over two bookings using temporal weather containment; the landing alternative makes the approver's certification itself part of the proposed physical support.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a venue manager, a dry-lawn objective and a second booking. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 make the approval plan increasingly impossible; logic 4, B2's timing becomes A3's pre-fall capture and B4's leak becomes A5's drought seal; relationship 4, B4 protects another paying wedding; heightening 4, A5 offers two-event protection using future drought and deferred billing; specificity 5, A1 establishes manager, wedding and lawn; brevity/wit 4, A5's invoice carries the future-weather premise into business procedure. Total 88. Five spoken ABABA turns; approval remains requested.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Using drought as a seal is a surreal analogy rather than a physical mechanism. The imagined containment remains clear, but A3 also introduces rain's learning as an additional assumption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D148-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"dcdb9bb559104a554342dbcb6ee1b7772c8f603172d74be3b43ba741f24049eb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requests sign-off; A3 converts absence into inspection success and A5 treats confidence as a construction material.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly uses B2's 'nothing there'; A5 addresses B4's standing question with a proposed support resource.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 raise credible inspection and usability concerns that shape A's justification.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 advances from an invisible structure to budgeting belief as its physical support.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's landing and stairs establish a construction approval encounter without extra exposition.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'No visible defects' earns its double meaning from B2's exact observation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Inspector, please approve our invisible landing. The museum opens Monday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's nothing supporting it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We've budgeted enough confidence to hold twenty visitors.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How am I supposed to certify confidence?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Sign under 'load-bearing.' Your professional certainty will support the inspectors too, so we won't need scaffolding for the next inspection.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A seeks formal construction approval through explanations that progress from an invisible structure to belief as material and certification as structural support.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Professional wordplay can simply evade inspection; A turns the inspector's requested certification method into an increasingly impossible means of making the project work.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 answers B2's support objection with budgeted confidence; A5 makes B4's certification problem solvable by a signature that itself bears weight.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The rain alternative offers a business bargain through future weather resources; this alternative recruits the inspector's authority as a literal component of the construction.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified a museum opening and inspector, replacing the detached budget line with a consequential certification request. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 expand impossible support while pursuing approval; logic 5, B2's support concern causes A3 and B4's certification question causes A5's load-bearing signature; relationship 4, B4 protects professional responsibility; heightening 4, A5 makes B's own certainty carry future inspectors; specificity 4, A1's Monday opening grounds the sign-off; brevity/wit 4, A5's scaffolding saving follows from literalized certification. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns; B retains the choice to refuse.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's quantified confidence is deliberately asserted rather than demonstrated. A5 must sound like an earnest proposed certification method, not a knowing joke about the inspector's liability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D149-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7e2786c26fa6f8aec4711c36527f31432528ecbb1fc642360ccd7c1cbb17ee69\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 assigns moon folding to B and keeps chair stacking; A5 defends that division when challenged.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's method question with a crescent crease; A5 addresses B4's complaint about the easier task.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 contests unequal labor, forcing A to justify retaining the achievable work.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's fairness objection into a rationale for preserving B's impossible responsibility.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 creates a cleanup division through moon folding and chair stacking, though the larger occasion is unstated.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'achievable work' candidly preserves the unfair allocation while sounding dutiful.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"For tonight's courtyard film, you fold the moon; I'll switch off the lamps.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How do I fold the moon?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Start with the crescent. It already has a crease.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll take the lamps. You handle the sky.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll do lamps, chairs and projector if you'll own the moon. Can I tell the audience we're waiting for your blackout?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A keeps the impossible component assigned to B by offering more achievable work in exchange and seeking explicit public accountability.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Merely offering absurd instructions does not secure responsibility; A bargains over ownership after B tries to reverse the assignments.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 connects moon folding to a shared blackout plan; A5 answers B4's reversal with a larger labor offer and a request to identify B as responsible for readiness.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative negotiates workload and audience-facing responsibility for a screening; the jar alternative exchanges practical assistance for a signed collector role tied to a refund.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced a courtyard screening so moon and lamps serve one objective. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1 assigns the impossible part and A5 seeks ownership; logic 5, B2's method question causes A3's crease and B4's reversal causes A5's expanded bargain; relationship 4, B4 contests the division while A5 offers additional work; heightening 4, A5 adds audience-facing accountability; specificity 4, A1 establishes tonight's film and lighting; brevity/wit 4, A5 treats cosmic blackout as one colleague's pending deliverable. Total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns; B's acceptance remains open.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's audience question can sound coercive. It should remain a sincere attempt to settle responsibility for starting the film, with the expanded workload offer available for B to negotiate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D149-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"df998078fd54facf55e17b73efd8b82314eb790cda555e693bd15aeda5fd453e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives B responsibility for jarring a lost hour; A5 refuses reassignment by claiming labeling duties.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's capacity objection with the lid; A5 uses B4's 'You do it' to defend A's separate role.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 directly tries to transfer the impossible work back, forcing A to preserve B's responsibility.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 upgrades labeling from busywork into protection against confusing yesterday with tomorrow.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a jar, a particular missing hour and a lunch deadline.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's lid adjustment treats B2's impossibility as a manageable opening-size problem.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"To claim our time-change refund, put yesterday's missing hour in this jar. I'll label it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"An hour won't fit.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll fetch a bigger jar. Can you manage the collecting?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I promised Accounts a full jar by lunch. Can you collect it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That makes you the collector. I'll put your deadline on the label; will you deliver the hour, or tell Accounts your refund needs cancelling?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses B's prior delivery promise to make B accept responsibility for collecting an impossible quantity while keeping ordinary preparation for A.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Assigning a nominal title can avoid securing actual work; A presses B to deliver the missing hour or personally withdraw the promised claim.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 offers a larger container while leaving collection with B; B4 reveals a delivery promise and requests a handoff, which A5 turns into responsibility for actual delivery or cancellation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The courtyard alternative offers additional labor and prospective audience accountability to win agreement. This alternative uses B's existing promise to Accounts as leverage, requiring B to own fulfillm