ce\": \"B2's shared ignorance prompts A3's experiment; B4's result leads to A5's precaution, though 'it' is ambiguous.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 shares uncertainty and B4 contributes an observation that advances their joint investigation.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 promises to learn 'the next rule' without specifying a new test or inference.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes suspended soup in an upside-down bowl, with spoon and sink supporting immediate play.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'owns down' is vivid, but A5's generic next-rule wording weakens the payoff.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"What keeps the soup inside that upside-down bowl?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've never seen it either.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then turn the spoon over. Let's test which thing owns down.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The soup followed the spoon.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then the spoon sets the direction. Point it into the sink before we try putting it down.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A tests the anomaly, infers a hidden organizing rule, and uses that inference to make the situation safer.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wondering at strangeness or requesting arbitrary experiments does not establish a practical explanatory rule.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A5 explicitly infers directional control from B4's observation and chooses a sink-directed precaution on that basis.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses a cooperative kitchen experiment to manage a physical hazard; alternative b tests a moving shadow and cautiously follows it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the kitchen